# Disable line-ending conversion for every file in this repo.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS — and it is not the reason the sibling registries give.
#
# The skills registry turns conversion off to protect a `contentHash` taken over
# SKILL.md. There is no such file here. The reason here is the NDJSON in `data/`.
#
# Two gates depend on those files being byte-identical wherever they are checked
# out. `build-dist --check` builds twice and compares a sha256 over every byte it
# is about to publish, and the publish workflow cross-checks the record count in
# the built index against `data/export-manifest.json`. Both are written on macOS
# and both are enforced on a Linux runner. If git rewrote line endings on
# checkout, a 69,052-line file would be a different 69,052 lines on the runner
# than on the machine that produced it, the digests would disagree for a reason
# nobody could see in a diff, and the honest conclusion — "the build is not
# deterministic" — would be wrong.
